#EXTINF:2317 group-title="Mark Twain",Mark Twains Autobiography Volume Ii — Mark Twain · Thursday- March 29- 1906 - Clemens as apprentice to Ament.--Wilhelm H's dinner.--Printing of Rev. Campbell's sermon.--Orion buys Hannibal Journal- goes to Muscatine- Iowa- and marries.--Clemens visits St. Louis- New York- Philadelphia- Washington- &amp; to Muscatine to work with Orion's --gets Horace Bixby to train him as pilot--starts with Orion for Nevada. - Read by John Greenman - Duration 00:38:37
